fuzzy-archer (the Bootstrap skin) 4.5 shades its charts by day/night using
the skyfield Python library and a JPL ephemeris file named by the skin's
[Skyfield] ephemeris option (de440s.bsp). Despite the section name, this is
fuzzy-archer's own setting; it is unrelated to the weewx-skyfield extension
(user.wxskyfield), which ships its own ephemeris.

Upstream locates the file at
    os.path.join(WEEWX_ROOT, SQLITE_ROOT, 'skyfield')
falling back to SQLITE_ROOT = '.' when unset. An absolute SQLITE_ROOT
discards WEEWX_ROOT, so the directory depends on the database settings:
    no SQLITE_ROOT (add-on template)  -> /opt/weewx-data/skyfield
    SQLITE_ROOT = archive (stock)     -> /opt/weewx-data/archive/skyfield
    SQLITE_ROOT = /var/lib/weewx      -> /var/lib/weewx/skyfield
It then downloads the file there (32 MB) if missing, and creates the
directory with os.mkdir, which raises FileNotFoundError when the parent
(e.g. /var/lib/weewx) does not exist.

Add a [Skyfield] data_dir option, joined to WEEWX_ROOT with os.path.join
(an absolute value is used as-is), and set it in the Bootstrap skin.conf
to the directory the image ships the ephemeris in:
    os.path.join('/opt/weewx-data', 'ephemeris') = /opt/weewx-data/ephemeris
Unset keeps upstream's location. Create the directory with os.makedirs.

--- a/bin/user/jsonengine.py
+++ b/bin/user/jsonengine.py
@@ -270,13 +270,20 @@
         if 'skyfield' not in sys.modules or not self.show_daynight:
             return []
 
-        sqlite_root = self.config_dict.get('DatabaseTypes',configobj.ConfigObj()).get('SQLite',configobj.ConfigObj()).get('SQLITE_ROOT','.')
-        path = os.path.join(
-            self.config_dict.get('WEEWX_ROOT','.'),
-            sqlite_root,
-            'skyfield'
-        )
-        if not os.path.isdir(path): os.mkdir(path)
+        # [Skyfield] data_dir: directory holding the ephemeris, joined to
+        # WEEWX_ROOT (an absolute value is used as-is). Unset keeps upstream's
+        # SQLITE_ROOT-based location.
+        data_dir = self.skin_dict['Skyfield'].get('data_dir')
+        if data_dir:
+            path = os.path.join(self.config_dict.get('WEEWX_ROOT','.'), data_dir)
+        else:
+            sqlite_root = self.config_dict.get('DatabaseTypes',configobj.ConfigObj()).get('SQLite',configobj.ConfigObj()).get('SQLITE_ROOT','.')
+            path = os.path.join(
+                self.config_dict.get('WEEWX_ROOT','.'),
+                sqlite_root,
+                'skyfield'
+            )
+        os.makedirs(path, exist_ok=True)
 
         events = SunEvents(start, end, lon, lat, int(altitude_m), path, self.skin_dict['Skyfield']['ephemeris']).get_transits(self.transition_angle)
         if events is None:
--- a/skins/Bootstrap/skin.conf
+++ b/skins/Bootstrap/skin.conf
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@
 
 [Skyfield]
     ephemeris = de440s.bsp # https://rhodesmill.org/skyfield/planets.html#choosing-an-ephemeris
+    # ha-weewx: os.path.join(WEEWX_ROOT, data_dir) = /opt/weewx-data/ephemeris,
+    # where the add-on image ships de440s.bsp (no download at report time).
+    data_dir = ephemeris
 
 [Units]
     [[TimeFormats]]
